      "Title": "Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameSession",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameSession.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">A live game between one human, always South, and three <xref href=\"Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Strategy.SimpleAiStrategy\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>\nseats. It is what every Hawsey UI drives: the UI calls the human's moves and the\nAI-advance methods, and redraws on <xref href=\"Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameSession.StateChanged\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>. The AI moves are\npaced so a person can follow them.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameState.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameState.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameState",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameState.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">A snapshot of the entire game state at a point in time. Each method on\n<xref href=\"Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameEngine\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> returns a freshly-constructed instance rather than mutating\nthe previous state, so callers should treat the exposed <xref href=\"Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameState.Hands\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and\n<xref href=\"Wolfgang.Hawsey.Engine.Game.GameState.CompletedTricks\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> collections as read-only — mutating them is unsupported\nand can corrupt subsequent engine transitions.</p>\n"
    },
